#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
aq-gate-checkout — Atomic check-out and mutual exclusion for validation gates.

Prevents multi-agent race conditions (e.g. Codex, Antigravity, Claude, Local Qwen)
when invoking heavyweight validation gates like tier0-validation-gate.sh, qa-phase0,
or pre-deploy validation.

Features:
- CAS / Exclusive lock via fcntl.flock on .agent/collaboration/gate-checkouts/<gate>.lock
- Lease JSON record in .agent/collaboration/gate-checkouts/<gate>.json with holder PID,
  agent name, task, hostname, timestamp, and TTL.
- Dead-PID auto-reclaim: if the holder process crashed or terminated without releasing,
  the stale lease is cleaned up immediately without waiting.
- Graceful polling with informative progress: when a gate is held by another active agent,
  waits up to --wait seconds (default: 300) with status messages, avoiding lock thrashing.
- Auto-release context runner: `aq-gate-checkout run -- <cmd>` handles signals (SIGINT, SIGTERM)
  and guarantees lease release on exit.
"""

